---
// STORY-ONLY wrapper for the member's card (specs/concepts/member-card.md).
// Nothing in the app imports it.
//
// The shipped surfaces embed the card as an image pointing at
// `/medlemsbevis/<token>/kort.svg` (see MemberCardFigure.astro), and Storybook
// serves no such address — a story of that component would show a broken image
// icon and prove nothing. What actually needs reviewing is the artwork, and
// `memberCardSvg` is a pure function, so this renders its real output inline.
// Same drawing, same code path, no server.
//
// **What Storybook shows is not pixel-identical to what gets shared.** Here a
// BROWSER draws the SVG, applying Fraunces' variable weights, so the secondary
// lines come out light. The card people actually receive — the og:image, the
// receipt attachment — is rasterized by resvg, which does not apply variable
// axes and renders every line at the font's default (heavy) instance. So judge
// layout, wrapping and hierarchy-by-size here, and check WEIGHT against the
// real thing: `/medlemsbevis/<token>/kort.png` (see qr-codes.md).
import { type MemberCardOptions, memberCardSvg } from "@stottemedlem/qr";

type Props = MemberCardOptions;
const svg = memberCardSvg(Astro.props);
---

<figure class="member-card">
  <Fragment set:html={svg} />
</figure>

<style>
  .member-card {
    margin: 0;
    /* Roughly the phone width the card is drawn for — judging an upright card
     * stretched across a desktop story pane tells you nothing useful. */
    max-width: 24rem;
  }
  .member-card :global(svg) {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }
</style>
